Yeah.

1507
01:05:22.480 --> 01:05:23.400
She is in tears.

1508
01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:29.960
Michael thinks he's finally made a breakthrough until she reveals that she's really crying about

1509
01:05:29.960 --> 01:05:31.000
her plans with Ryan.

1510
01:05:32.520 --> 01:05:34.420
I have a question about this scene.

1511
01:05:34.520 --> 01:05:34.680
Okay.

1512
01:05:35.900 --> 01:05:38.560
What is up with this second copier in the annex?

1513
01:05:38.880 --> 01:05:40.180
Is it always there?

1514
01:05:40.420 --> 01:05:42.220
I have never seen it before.

1515
01:05:42.800 --> 01:05:43.860
What is happening?

1516
01:05:44.040 --> 01:05:47.220
I think they just rolled it in from the bullpen for the scene.

1517
01:05:48.020 --> 01:05:52.580
I feel like they did, and they did it because in the background, in the break room, Dwight

1518
01:05:52.580 --> 01:05:53.380
is in there.

1519
01:05:53.560 --> 01:05:58.300
You can see him over Kelly's shoulder trying to shove this bird into an empty soda can.

1520
01:05:58.500 --> 01:06:02.540
I feel like that's why they had to put the copier there to combine these two moments,

1521
01:06:02.540 --> 01:06:04.880
to have a reason for Michael to be back there.

1522
01:06:05.020 --> 01:06:05.180
Right.

1523
01:06:05.200 --> 01:06:07.720
And for him to see over his shoulder and all of that.

1524
01:06:07.900 --> 01:06:08.340
Exactly.

1525
01:06:08.580 --> 01:06:10.840
That copier did not live there in that hallway.

1526
01:06:11.080 --> 01:06:12.440
They just shoved it there.

1527
01:06:12.560 --> 01:06:12.780
Yeah.

1528
01:06:12.780 --> 01:06:14.140
I did not think so.

1529
01:06:14.140 --> 01:06:16.200
I feel like I will track this.

1530
01:06:16.340 --> 01:06:19.720
It's going to be a soft track, but I am going to look for this copier more.

1531
01:06:19.860 --> 01:06:25.040
I think it should be a very soft track because I would be bold enough to say I think it might

1532
01:06:25.040 --> 01:06:26.760
be the only time it's in the annex.

1533
01:06:26.760 --> 01:06:33.540
I know that's setting myself up for some fan mail of Angela actually in season eight, but

1534
01:06:33.540 --> 01:06:37.780
I'm just saying I don't think that copier visits the annex very often.

1535
01:06:38.340 --> 01:06:42.660
Guys, if you're watching another episode and you see that copier, write to us.

1536
01:06:42.840 --> 01:06:48.500
You can go to our website, officeladies.com, and submit questions or comments or write to

1537
01:06:48.500 --> 01:06:50.760
us at officeladies at earwolf.com.

1538
01:06:50.860 --> 01:06:51.380
Okay, here we go.

1539
01:06:51.420 --> 01:06:52.060
We want to know.

1540
01:06:52.200 --> 01:06:52.940
We want to know.

1541
01:06:52.940 --> 01:06:57.920
All right, but this leads us into one of my favorite Dwight Talking Heads where he explains

1542
01:06:57.920 --> 01:07:03.800
he's justifying why is he shoving this bird into a can, and it's because he grew up on

1543
01:07:03.800 --> 01:07:04.300
a farm.

1544
01:07:04.520 --> 01:07:04.660
Yeah.

1545
01:07:05.080 --> 01:07:09.040
And guys, they reburied his grandfather in an old oil drum.

1546
01:07:11.000 --> 01:07:12.080
Okay, hold on.

1547
01:07:12.200 --> 01:07:16.680
I mean, the same grandfather that was buried in the suit that he wore?

1548
01:07:16.840 --> 01:07:17.560
Like, what's happening?

1549
01:07:17.660 --> 01:07:19.880
How many times has this guy been brought up out of the ground?

1550
01:07:20.060 --> 01:07:22.140
This is one of my favorite things about our show.

1551
01:07:22.140 --> 01:07:23.200
Teresa S.

1552
01:07:23.480 --> 01:07:23.980
also loves it.

1553
01:07:24.120 --> 01:07:29.180
She wrote in to say, in Casino Night, Dwight says that his grandfather was buried in the

1554
01:07:29.180 --> 01:07:30.280
tuxedo he's wearing.

1555
01:07:30.520 --> 01:07:30.640
Yeah.

1556
01:07:31.340 --> 01:07:35.400
And in Grief Counseling, he said his grandfather was reburied in an oil drum.

1557
01:07:35.580 --> 01:07:35.700
Yeah.

1558
01:07:36.360 --> 01:07:36.840
Reburied?

1559
01:07:36.980 --> 01:07:37.180
What?

1560
01:07:37.180 --> 01:07:38.660
She wrote, reburied.

1561
01:07:38.700 --> 01:07:39.200
What happened?

1562
01:07:39.680 --> 01:07:42.260
What is the story behind Dwight's grandfather?

1563
01:07:42.440 --> 01:07:44.000
Was he exhumed for some reason?

1564
01:07:44.320 --> 01:07:47.600
And did Dwight take the tuxedo off his dead grandfather?

1565
01:07:47.880 --> 01:07:48.000
Yeah.

1566
01:07:48.020 --> 01:07:49.340
Before reburying him?

1567
01:07:49.440 --> 01:07:49.880
And then fold him up?

1568
01:07:49.880 --> 01:07:50.780
It sounds like it.

1569
01:07:50.780 --> 01:07:53.240
Then he folded him up and tried to shove him in a drum.

1570
01:07:53.500 --> 01:07:55.600
Teresa, that's exactly what it sounds like.

1571
01:07:55.920 --> 01:07:58.420
This is some of my favorite writing on our show.

1572
01:07:58.560 --> 01:08:02.800
In that moment in Casino Night, when Dwight just says he's wearing a tuxedo, my grandfather

1573
01:08:02.800 --> 01:08:03.600
was buried in it.

1574
01:08:03.740 --> 01:08:04.340
That's it.

1575
01:08:04.420 --> 01:08:05.540
We say no more about it.

1576
01:08:05.680 --> 01:08:09.940
And then three episodes later, he's like, when my grandfather was reburied.

1577
01:08:10.780 --> 01:08:13.520
And it's like, slowly, it's all coming together.

1578
01:08:14.340 --> 01:08:15.000
Sort of.

1579
01:08:15.200 --> 01:08:15.600
Sort of.

1580
01:08:15.600 --> 01:08:16.300
Not completely.

1581
01:08:16.760 --> 01:08:19.480
It's one of my favorite bits of how our show is written.

1582
01:08:19.860 --> 01:08:21.700
So now we're at reception, right?

1583
01:08:21.880 --> 01:08:25.280
And Pam has prepared this really beautiful box for the bird funeral.

1584
01:08:25.480 --> 01:08:26.980
I mean, it is amazing.

1585
01:08:26.980 --> 01:08:28.460
The attention to detail.

1586
01:08:28.900 --> 01:08:32.180
She asked Dwight if he would perhaps want to play a song.

1587
01:08:32.300 --> 01:08:33.440
She's like, do you have your recorder?

1588
01:08:33.580 --> 01:08:35.900
He's like, always, always has.

1589
01:08:36.160 --> 01:08:36.280
Always.

1590
01:08:36.500 --> 01:08:36.640
Always.

1591
01:08:38.060 --> 01:08:41.740
And, you know, Pam has this really sweet talking head where she's like, well, you know

1592
01:08:41.740 --> 01:08:41.980
what?

1593
01:08:42.160 --> 01:08:46.000
I didn't anticipate I'd be throwing a bird funeral today, but you never know, working

1594
01:08:46.000 --> 01:08:46.380
here.

1595
01:08:46.560 --> 01:08:47.180
That's right.

1596
01:08:47.320 --> 01:08:49.120
We had a fan question from Andrew S.

1597
01:08:49.260 --> 01:08:51.800
Did Jenna make the box for the bird funeral herself,

1598
01:08:51.800 --> 01:08:53.820
or was that a Phil Shea creation?

1599
01:08:54.180 --> 01:08:56.720
Either way, how was it constructed?

1600
01:08:57.020 --> 01:08:58.720
Well, guys, I did not make it.

1601
01:08:59.060 --> 01:09:00.260
Phil Shea made it.

1602
01:09:00.380 --> 01:09:06.020
He said he actually made a few options and presented them again to Jen and Roger and Greg.

1603
01:09:06.020 --> 01:09:10.620
They picked the one that they liked, and then Phil had to make multiples of it because,

1604
01:09:10.800 --> 01:09:12.820
you know, it gets set on fire.

1605
01:09:13.120 --> 01:09:15.040
So he had to make a whole bunch of those.

1606
01:09:15.400 --> 01:09:18.640
I looked it up in the script, and it was described in the script.

1607
01:09:18.680 --> 01:09:20.780
So here's what Phil had to go off of.

1608
01:09:21.000 --> 01:09:26.540
It said, it is a hollowed out tissue box with tissue padding in the center for the bird to

1609
01:09:26.540 --> 01:09:32.200
lie on, and the outside is decorated in tissue paper and has a tiny little toothpick cross.

1610
01:09:32.600 --> 01:09:35.400
My favorite part are the handles.

1611
01:09:36.020 --> 01:09:38.800
The handles made out of the pencils.

1612
01:09:39.180 --> 01:09:40.720
So that was a Phil edition.

1613
01:09:41.100 --> 01:09:42.620
That was just Phil.

1614
01:09:43.060 --> 01:09:43.840
Yeah, yeah.

1615
01:09:44.040 --> 01:09:50.500
He needed to make sure that tiny bird casket had little bars for the pallbearers.

1616
01:09:50.920 --> 01:09:51.760
That's right.

1617
01:09:52.060 --> 01:09:53.700
The tiny pallbearers.

1618
01:09:53.820 --> 01:09:54.240
Yes.

1619
01:09:54.420 --> 01:09:57.620
We are going to wrap things up in Stanford now, guys.

1620
01:09:57.900 --> 01:09:58.960
Jim found the chips.

1621
01:09:59.460 --> 01:10:01.000
He left them on her desk.

1622
01:10:01.100 --> 01:10:02.660
He's quite pleased with himself.

1623
01:10:02.660 --> 01:10:09.720
Yeah, I really wanted my mom to record a sting that said, flirty Jim, but we couldn't get

1624
01:10:09.720 --> 01:10:10.260
it together.

1625
01:10:10.720 --> 01:10:13.120
Aw, well, these scenes drove people crazy.

1626
01:10:13.540 --> 01:10:17.600
I went back and looked at some of the comments from when this aired.

1627
01:10:18.240 --> 01:10:20.720
Oh, here is what they said.

1628
01:10:21.540 --> 01:10:24.680
D-Temp said, I feel kind of weird about Jim and Karen.

1629
01:10:25.540 --> 01:10:28.260
But Hartman said, the Karen thing?

1630
01:10:28.520 --> 01:10:30.420
Why, oh, why am I liking it?

1631
01:10:30.500 --> 01:10:31.240
But I am.

1632
01:10:31.760 --> 01:10:31.820
Whoa.

1633
01:10:31.820 --> 01:10:35.060
Oh, I remember people freaking out about it.

1634
01:10:35.940 --> 01:10:39.300
Well, Keely said, Jim and Karen have great chemistry.

1635
01:10:40.020 --> 01:10:44.460
And Mandy said, okay, I'm sorry, I can't believe there are actually people out there

1636
01:10:44.460 --> 01:10:46.500
who are okay with Jim hooking up with Karen.

1637
01:10:46.680 --> 01:10:47.580
That's what I remember.

1638
01:10:48.640 --> 01:10:49.840
But Kim E.

1639
01:10:50.080 --> 01:10:50.820
said this.

1640
01:10:51.760 --> 01:10:52.080
Hmm.

1641
01:10:52.480 --> 01:10:54.800
Jim likes to buy chips for all his ladies.

1642
01:10:56.260 --> 01:10:57.860
And I'm with you, Kim.

1643
01:10:58.980 --> 01:11:01.880
As Pam, I'm like, oh, is this what you do?

1644
01:11:02.320 --> 01:11:05.240
You just find all the girls their favorite chips?

1645
01:11:05.620 --> 01:11:06.860
Yeah, that's his game.

1646
01:11:07.720 --> 01:11:08.960
Are we saying that right?

1647
01:11:09.220 --> 01:11:09.600
Oh.

1648
01:11:09.800 --> 01:11:10.480
Is that your game?

1649
01:11:10.480 --> 01:11:10.960
You and I?

1650
01:11:11.220 --> 01:11:13.160
I 100% doubt we are.

1651
01:11:13.160 --> 01:11:14.680
Oh, Sam's giving us an okay.

1652
01:11:14.680 --> 01:11:15.480
Sam gave us an okay.

1653
01:11:15.640 --> 01:11:16.580
That's his game.

1654
01:11:17.340 --> 01:11:18.000
All right.

1655
01:11:18.140 --> 01:11:19.820
Should we go to this bird funeral, Angela?

1656
01:11:20.100 --> 01:11:20.980
I can't wait.

1657
01:11:21.600 --> 01:11:22.880
Please take me there.

1658
01:11:22.880 --> 01:11:27.840
Well, we're out in the driveway, really, next to the warehouse.

1659
01:11:28.200 --> 01:11:33.640
This was an actual parking lot that we used, and it was right next to the warehouse, and

1660
01:11:33.640 --> 01:11:34.780
that's where we filmed this.

1661
01:11:35.780 --> 01:11:38.760
Michael is very moved by Pam's beautiful coffin.

1662
01:11:39.140 --> 01:11:45.140
It starts with Pam saying a few words about the bird, but we slowly realize that Pam is

1663
01:11:45.140 --> 01:11:48.100
speaking about the bird, but she's speaking to Michael.

1664
01:11:48.420 --> 01:11:51.200
About his feelings about death and loss.

1665
01:11:51.200 --> 01:11:53.560
And about his aloneness.

1666
01:11:54.280 --> 01:12:01.020
She talks a lot about how just because the bird was alone doesn't mean he was unloved,

1667
01:12:01.220 --> 01:12:05.260
that he was very loved and respected by the other birds.

1668
01:12:05.500 --> 01:12:06.980
And then she sings a song.

1669
01:12:07.180 --> 01:12:09.420
I was very surprised by this for Pam.

1670
01:12:09.680 --> 01:12:11.200
She really put herself out there.

1671
01:12:11.340 --> 01:12:13.320
She sings On the Wings of Love.

1672
01:12:13.600 --> 01:12:15.880
She's accompanied by Dwight on the recorder.

1673
01:12:16.500 --> 01:12:17.980
Michael is very moved.

1674
01:12:17.980 --> 01:12:18.980
He's holding hands.

1675
01:12:18.980 --> 01:12:19.840
He's swaying.

1676
01:12:19.980 --> 01:12:20.860
He's tearing up.

1677
01:12:21.100 --> 01:12:23.480
We got a lot of questions about this scene.

1678
01:12:24.260 --> 01:12:25.180
Richard H.

1679
01:12:25.420 --> 01:12:26.480
really covers them all.

1680
01:12:26.800 --> 01:12:29.820
He says, did Rain already know how to play the recorder?

1681
01:12:30.160 --> 01:12:32.440
Did Jenna sing the entire song?

1682
01:12:32.580 --> 01:12:35.100
Or did the singing end where the scene was cut?

1683
01:12:35.600 --> 01:12:38.640
He also wanted to know, did we rehearse our duet?

1684
01:12:39.400 --> 01:12:40.840
Here's what I can tell you.

1685
01:12:41.920 --> 01:12:44.000
Yes, Rain knew how to play the recorder.

1686
01:12:44.720 --> 01:12:46.940
Remember, he played it in Take Your Daughter to Work Day.

1687
01:12:46.980 --> 01:12:48.500
It was actually very good.

1688
01:12:48.840 --> 01:12:52.540
But listen to all of the instruments that Rain can play in real life, Angela.

1689
01:12:53.220 --> 01:13:04.640
He can play the recorder, piano, clarinet, saxophone, bassoon, guitar, drums, xylophone, bells, and a little tuba and baritone.

1690
01:13:04.760 --> 01:13:06.740
What are you, a one-man band, Rain?

1691
01:13:07.160 --> 01:13:08.320
He kind of is.

1692
01:13:08.320 --> 01:13:12.220
I knew you could play the bassoon because your book, The Bassoon King, is great.

1693
01:13:12.220 --> 01:13:13.360
So I knew that.

1694
01:13:13.760 --> 01:13:16.560
But I didn't know you were a walking one-man show.

1695
01:13:16.860 --> 01:13:19.320
Suffice it to say, Rain knew his stuff.

1696
01:13:20.000 --> 01:13:24.400
And we did rehearse, but just a little bit right before the scene.

1697
01:13:24.620 --> 01:13:26.200
Rain and I practiced separately.

1698
01:13:26.460 --> 01:13:29.520
I had listened to the song over and over again to memorize the words.

1699
01:13:29.720 --> 01:13:33.180
I had to sing the first verse through the chorus.

1700
01:13:33.940 --> 01:13:35.860
That's what I had to do over and over again.

1701
01:13:36.500 --> 01:13:37.920
I was so nervous.

1702
01:13:38.420 --> 01:13:40.120
Well, I thought you did fantastic.

1703
01:13:41.260 --> 01:13:42.020
Thank you.

1704
01:13:42.240 --> 01:13:44.420
I have a fan question from the scene, Jenna.

1705
01:13:45.220 --> 01:13:45.480
Okay.

1706
01:13:46.180 --> 01:13:51.240
So Chelsea wrote in and said, was Angela's A-man improvised?

1707
01:13:51.420 --> 01:13:55.840
A lot of people wrote in about this because it was so quick after Pam was done talking.

1708
01:13:55.980 --> 01:13:57.900
People wanted to know if I improvised that.

1709
01:13:58.080 --> 01:13:59.640
No, that was scripted.

1710
01:13:59.640 --> 01:14:03.280
And folks wanted to know why did Angela do it.

1711
01:14:03.400 --> 01:14:13.900
And I said, I think personally, the direction that, you know, they gave me was that Angela had had enough of this charade, this bird funeral.

1712
01:14:14.100 --> 01:14:15.480
Pam had gone on and on.

1713
01:14:15.600 --> 01:14:15.860
Enough.

1714
01:14:16.000 --> 01:14:16.240
Amen.

1715
01:14:16.480 --> 01:14:17.160
I'm done.

1716
01:14:17.580 --> 01:14:18.360
And that...

1717
01:14:18.360 --> 01:14:19.720
That's how you finish it.

1718
01:14:19.820 --> 01:14:20.180
Yes.

1719
01:14:20.460 --> 01:14:20.700
Amen.

1720
01:14:21.200 --> 01:14:21.600
I'm finished.

1721
01:14:21.820 --> 01:14:21.960
Amen.

1722
01:14:22.200 --> 01:14:22.720
Stop talking.

1723
01:14:23.460 --> 01:14:24.460
Yes, exactly.

1724
01:14:25.380 --> 01:14:27.460
Speaking of the script, I have a script catch.

1725
01:14:27.660 --> 01:14:27.800
Okay.

1726
01:14:27.800 --> 01:14:30.140
So, you know, in the scene, we set the box on fire.

1727
01:14:30.400 --> 01:14:33.360
In the shooting draft of the script, we buried the bird.

1728
01:14:34.060 --> 01:14:39.820
There was a scene where Michael and Dwight are digging a hole outside, and then we all gather around this hole.

1729
01:14:40.300 --> 01:14:43.160
And it got changed to fire, but I don't know why.

1730
01:14:43.160 --> 01:14:49.620
I think maybe, Angela, there was really no grass in this area that we shot.

1731
01:14:49.620 --> 01:14:50.480
We had no grass.

1732
01:14:50.680 --> 01:14:55.580
There was a hedge with maybe, like, I don't know, three feet of dirt.

1733
01:14:56.000 --> 01:14:57.780
Like, yeah, there was, I mean...

1734
01:14:57.800 --> 01:14:58.380
Not even.

1735
01:14:58.600 --> 01:15:06.080
There is a deleted scene where Michael and Dwight are trying to dig a hole there, and then the business on the other side yells at them, and they run away.

1736
01:15:06.820 --> 01:15:07.320
Oh!

1737
01:15:07.700 --> 01:15:08.160
Okay.

1738
01:15:08.480 --> 01:15:09.380
Well, there you go.

1739
01:15:09.880 --> 01:15:13.140
Well, we had another fan question about this fire, then.

1740
01:15:13.480 --> 01:15:17.360
Clara Johnson wants to know, did you actually set the bird on fire?

1741
01:15:18.180 --> 01:15:18.680
Yes.

1742
01:15:18.900 --> 01:15:20.480
Real fire, fake bird.

1743
01:15:20.700 --> 01:15:27.740
Kent told me they had to hire a special effects guy to oversee the fire and the extinguishing, and they had to get a special permit.

1744
01:15:27.800 --> 01:15:29.300
To be allowed to set the fire.

1745
01:15:29.700 --> 01:15:31.600
And he said we did three takes.

1746
01:15:32.180 --> 01:15:33.420
Three takes of the fire.

1747
01:15:33.720 --> 01:15:41.740
And Phil told me, though, that the special effects guys were worried that the fake dead bird might give off toxic fumes when it burned.

1748
01:15:41.740 --> 01:15:46.380
So we, they actually took it out of the box and just put a wad of toilet paper in there.

1749
01:15:46.720 --> 01:15:48.700
Oh, not toilet paper.

1750
01:15:49.580 --> 01:15:50.500
I know.

1751
01:15:51.060 --> 01:15:51.760
Too soon.

1752
01:15:51.760 --> 01:15:51.900
I know.

1753
01:15:52.100 --> 01:15:52.960
Too soon, Angela.

1754
01:15:53.260 --> 01:15:53.720
Too soon.

1755
01:15:55.200 --> 01:15:59.720
And then, finally, we had a fan catch from Peter K.

